sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Confuciusornis sanctus Turing wavelength at 143.4 µm (Yixian Fm, 125.0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 63.3/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 implements Schnakenberg kinetics whose analytic critical wavelength is 143.4 µm (log10 size -3.843) at the Yixian 125.0 Ma horizon. The periodic collar of 1147.2 µm selects Fourier mode 8. The equal-diffusion control is analytic only (σ_max < 0). The comparison figure shows the CC BY-SA 4.0 Senckenberg slab beside the stripe field; the GIF is the unfitted stripe field (12 frames, 640×480). No diffusion-ratio sweep, spatial ablation, specimen CV segmentation, or Pearson/RMSE/KS fit yet. Overall 63.3/100 (faithfulness 55.4, reproducibility 81.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit fbd09a11bf97bd7e131df1afb92f62af0b4105ba; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 82, Morphological realism / specimen match 48, Parameter expressivity 38, Morphometric validation 44, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 76, Reproducibility package 80. Output judged: docs/media/confuciusornis_sanctus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at fbd09a11bf97bd7e131df1afb92f62af0b4105ba, image/png, 472183 B, 1512×552 px, artifact_sha256 efc52c8d4fd1f391fd2c11c84b3dbb4c2dc0cc6333ba2bb360b8750fbaddb4e9 (sha256 efc52c8d4fd1f391fd2c11c84b3dbb4c2dc0cc6333ba2bb360b8750fbaddb4e9), spec_fingerprint eefa4e9a500552e28e1fe0176dd6aca52038d5438def2a8270217cfbd375bf34. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: eefa4e9a500552e28e1fe0176dd6aca52038d5438def2a8270217cfbd375bf34; artifact_sha256: efc52c8d4fd1f391fd2c11c84b3dbb4c2dc0cc6333ba2bb360b8750fbaddb4e9; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/confuciusornis_sanctus_turing_wavelength_s0/confuciusornis_sanctus_specimen.jpg=9e83715a2090a049..., datasets/confuciusornis_sanctus_turing_wavelength_s0/confuciusornis_sanctus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=95376a32ced97ca5..., datasets/confuciusornis_sanctus_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=969b2a6a15f61ba8...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) critical wavenumber from the dispersion relation | Within-feather pigment bars and spots are a reaction-diffusion pattern (Prum & Williamson 2002) | Barb-ridge spacing is an activator-inhibitor process (Harris et al. 2005) | Confuciusornis sanctus is a beaked pygostylian with ribbon rectrices and preserved feather pigment; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters a=0.08, b=1.12, Du=0.5, Dv=6.0 chosen so λ_c = 143.4 µm | Spectral split-step on a periodic 8-wavelength collar; transfer_boundary: The numerical kinetics are a carrier of k_c, not a parameter table from the feather papers | 143.4 µm is the slot scale, not a new measurement of a fossil barb; does_not_claim: That the Senckenberg slab outline is a Turing pattern | That melanosome length equals 143.4 µm." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [morphometric_validation/morphometric-validation, pressure P=3.55]: Add Pearson r, RMSE, and KS, plus a spatial ablation.",
            "open need [parameter_sweep/parameter-expressivity, pressure P=2.9]: Sweep Dv/Du across the Turing threshold and show λ_c moving.",
            "open need [specimen_comparison/specimen-match, pressure P=4.2]: Segment the CC BY-SA slab and fit the animated last frame to its orientation, radial FFT, and coherency.",
            "remediation needed: R1 parameter-regime sweep: vary Dv/Du and record λ_c and the selected mode",
            "remediation needed: R2 negative control: spatial equal-diffusion ablation, not only the analytic σ ceiling",
            "remediation needed: R3 segment the real Senckenberg specimen (foreground, coherency, circularity, radial wavelength) and register the GIF's last frame to that photograph",
            "remediation needed: R4 goodness-of-fit: Pearson r, RMSE, and a KS statistic against an empirical series, with at least one non-circular specimen metric" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.633"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, Pass 1; second assessor not run)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

